  "title": "Learning Tools Interoperability (LTI) Integration and Management Cluster",
  "description": "The Xikolo platform features a robust Learning Tools Interoperability (LTI) integration, functioning both as an LTI consumer for launching external tools and receiving grades, and as a comprehensive system for managing LTI tool providers. This merged cluster, encompassing various components and functionalities, ensures seamless interaction with third-party educational tools and services, enhancing the platform's extensibility and educational offerings. The system's capabilities span from detailed provider configuration to handling complex grading workflows and secure content management.",
  "functional_domain": "Learning Tools Interoperability (LTI) Integration and Management",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "LTI Provider Management",
      "description": "This section details the management of LTI providers, which can be configured at both global and course-specific levels. Key components involved include `LtiProvidersController` and `Admin::LtiProvidersController`.",
      "sub_sections": [
        {
          "title": "Global LTI Provider Management",
          "content": "Administrators manage global LTI providers via the `Admin::LtiProvidersController` (Source: app/controllers/admin/lti_providers_controller.rb). This controller facilitates standard CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for `Lti::Provider` records. Access is secured by the `lti.provider.manage` permission (Source: app/controllers/admin/lti_providers_controller.rb), typically assigned to `xikolo.admins` (Source: services/account/lib/tasks/permissions/lti.yml). The creation and update processes utilize the `Course::Admin::LtiProviderForm` (Source: app/forms/course/admin/lti_provider_form.rb), which defines and validates attributes such as name, domain, consumer key, and shared secret. A critical aspect of this management is the handling of data privacy, highlighted by a confirmation modal for setting the `privacy` option to 'unprotected' (Source: integration/features/xikolo/global/admin/lti_provider.feature). The `PrivacyAlert` component (Source: C19_LTI_Integration) is likely involved in presenting these privacy considerations to the administrator. The listing and viewing of providers are facilitated by functionality akin to an `LtiProvidersIndex` (Source: C19_LTI_Integration), which is part of the `LtiProvidersController`'s read operations."
        },
        {
          "title": "Course-Specific LTI Provider Management",
          "content": "Within the context of individual courses, LTI providers can be managed by course administrators or users possessing the `lti.provider.manage` permission. This is handled by the `LtiProvidersController` (Source: app/controllers/lti_providers_controller.rb, C19_LTI_Integration), which inherits from `Abstract::FrontendController` and leverages `CourseContextHelper`. It enables the creation, update, and deletion of `Lti::Provider` instances specifically tied to a `course_id`. Modifying the `privacy` setting for course-specific LTI providers requires the `lti.provider.edit_privacy_mode` permission (Source: app/controllers/lti_providers_controller.rb, services/account/lib/tasks/permissions/lti.yml)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "LTI Consumer Functionality",
      "description": "The platform's LTI consumer capabilities are primarily managed by the `LtiController` (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb, main_app_lti_integration_web, C19_LTI_Integration), which orchestrates tool launches, grading callbacks, and returns from external LTI tools.",
      "sub_sections": [
        {
          "title": "Tool Launch",
          "content": "When a user interacts with a `Course::Item` configured as an LTI exercise, the `LtiController#tool_launch` action is invoked (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb). The `LtiExerciseItemPresenter` (Source: app/presenters/lti_exercise_item_presenter.rb, main_app_lti_integration_web) dynamically determines the display method, either an introductory page with a launch button or an embedded iframe, based on the LTI provider's `presentation_mode` and whether it's an initial click. Subsequently, the `Course::LtiLaunchPresenter` prepares the necessary LTI launch parameters for the external tool (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Tool Grading",
          "content": "External LTI tools communicate grading results to the `LtiController#tool_grading` endpoint (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb). This action is specifically configured to bypass CSRF verification and standard authentication middleware, recognizing its role in backend-to-backend communication. The core logic for processing these callbacks is encapsulated within the `LtiController::ToolGrading` service object (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb, main_app_lti_integration_web, C19_LTI_Integration).\n\n**`LtiController::ToolGrading` Responsibilities:** This service object is critical for:\n*   **Request Validation:** It verifies the `lis_result_sourcedid` (grading ID), authorizes the request using `IMS::LTI::ToolConsumer` with the `Lti::Provider`'s consumer key and shared secret, and checks for session expiry (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb).\n*   **Grade Submission:** Upon successful validation, it submits the received score to the `Lti::Gradebook` (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb).\n*   **Event Publishing:** An LTI submission event is published to the `xikolo.web.exp_event.create` topic via `Msgr` for analytics and tracking, including `course_id`, `score`, `provider_name`, and `user_ip` (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb).\n*   **Response Generation:** An XML response is generated using `IMS::LTI::OutcomeResponse` to acknowledge the grading operation to the external LTI tool (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Tool Return",
          "content": "Following an interaction with an LTI tool, the `LtiController#tool_return` action (Source: app/controllers/lti_controller.rb) manages redirects and displays any informational (`lti_msg`) or error (`lti_errormsg`) messages returned by the LTI tool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "LTI Grade Processing",
      "description": "Once an LTI grade is successfully submitted and recorded, for instance, by `LtiController::ToolGrading`, the `Lti::PublishGradeJob` (Source: app/jobs/lti/publish_grade_job.rb, main_app_lti_integration_web) is enqueued as a background job. This job is responsible for locating the relevant `Lti::Grade` record and invoking its `publish!` method, thereby integrating the grade into the platform's comprehensive course progress and grading system."
    },
    {
      "title": "LTI Exercise Content Management",
      "description": "The `Lti::Exercise::Store` operation (Source: app/operations/lti/exercise/store.rb) is specifically designed for managing the content, particularly the `instructions`, of `Lti::Exercise` objects. This operation utilizes `Xikolo::S3::TextWithUploadsProcessor` to handle text content that may contain embedded references to files stored in S3. It configures necessary S3 upload parameters (e.g., bucket, key, ACL) and ensures that obsolete S3 files are scheduled for deletion via `S3FileDeletionJob` after a delay, providing fault tolerance for potentially slow connections."
    }
  ],
